# AMD EPYC LIKWID-only PMU

**Activation:** `alwaysApply: false` — when triggers in `agent-discipline-core.mdc` match, **Read this file before editing**.

## Law

- EPYC Rome/Milan/Genoa/Turin core + DF + RAPL go through **LIKWID** only.
- DF `st_name`s are family-named: `amd_x86_uncore_df_{rome,milan,genoa,turin}` (IMC pattern).
- **No MSR fallback** if LIKWID init/read fails — disable the type.
- Do not reintroduce `amd64_pmc` / native MSR `amd64_df` / emit `amd_x86_pmc` or bare `amd_x86_uncore_df`.
- CPUID allowlists are **EPYC server model ranges** only (`amd_cpuid_match.c`).

See [LIKWID_MIGRATION.md](../LIKWID_MIGRATION.md) AMD section.

## Overlap

- **monitor-emitted-variable-naming** — generation in type name
- **monitor-consumer-schema-migration** — DF type split needs consumer follow-up
